What? I thought Stormbringer is one of the best weapons. True it does not
drain life from demons and undeads, but undeads aren't hard too kill and
Stormbringer prevents the life drain. You met powerful demons only in the hell,
by that time, my armors are usually good enough (-20 or better) that it
doesn't matter that much. Besides, Stormbringer is an evil weapon and Excalibur
is a lawful weapon, so it make sense that Excalibur is better against demons
than Stormbringer. I prefer Stormbringer over Excalibur because it can drain
life from most monsters. Stormbringer does +5 to hit, +1d2 extra damage to all
monsters, pluse 1d8 extra and reduce monster level by 1 if appicable.
It is also the best weapon against the Wizard of Yendor.

The only weapon I would choose over Stormbringer is probably Mjollnir, but
Mjollnir is much harder to get. (Even if you are lawful, you need to 
sacrafice a long time to get Mjollnir, but when you are chaotic, you get
Stormbringer fairly easy once you find an altar.)


